cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ShortSeq in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "ShortSeq: A benchmark for foundation model evaluation on short time series"
abstract: >-
  ShortSeq evaluates classical, machine-learning, and foundation-model
  forecasters on short time series, where the sample sizes that favour
  large pretrained models are absent. It provides a pip-installable
  package, a rolling one-step-ahead evaluation protocol with no
  look-ahead, and statistical significance testing (Diebold-Mariano with
  Bonferroni correction; Friedman omnibus with Nemenyi post-hoc).

  The benchmark covers 368 series drawn from ten public sources, split
  into a short stratum (n < 200, 199 series) and a long stratum
  (n >= 200, 169 series) that are analysed separately and never pooled.

  Note that ShortSeq redistributes loaders, evaluation code, and computed
  results, but not the underlying raw data: several constituent sources
  are governed by licences that prohibit redistribution and must be
  obtained by the user from their original providers.
authors:
